{"name":"Camel","hex":"#c69f59","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Camel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A river in Cornwall, England, which flows into the Atlantic Ocean near Padstow."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cigarette of a popular American brand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Camel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Camel","blocks":[{"text":"A camel is an even-toed ungulate in the genus Camelus that bears distinctive fatty deposits known as \"humps\" on its back. Camels have long been domesticated and, as livestock, they provide food and textiles. Camels are working animals especially suited to their desert habitat and are a vital means of transport for passengers and cargo. There are three surviving species of camel. The one-humped dromedary makes up 94% of the world's camel population, and the two-humped Bactrian camel makes up 6%. The wild Bactrian camel is a distinct species that is not ancestral to the domestic Bactrian camel, and is now endangered, with around 1,000 individuals and a continuing decline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/07._Camel_Profile%2C_near_Silverton%2C_NSW%2C_07.07.2007.jpg/330px-07._Camel_Profile%2C_near_Silverton%2C_NSW%2C_07.07.2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel","wikidata":"Q7375"},{"title":"Camel (cigarette)","blocks":[{"text":"Camel is an American brand of cigarettes, currently owned and manufactured by the R. J. Reynolds Tobacco Company in the United States and by Japan Tobacco outside the U.S. Most recently Camel cigarettes contain a blend of Turkish tobacco and Virginia tobacco. Winston-Salem, North Carolina, the city where R. J. Reynolds was founded, is nicknamed \"Camel City\" because of the brand's popularity."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/34/Camel_cigarettes_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel_(cigarette)","wikidata":"Q878241"},{"title":"Camel (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Camel is a color that resembles the color of the hair of a camel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Camelcalf-feeding.jpg/330px-Camelcalf-feeding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Camel_(color)","wikidata":"Q17082553"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Camels_by_country_per_capita.png/500px-Camels_by_country_per_capita.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Camels_by_country_per_capita.png/1280px-Camels_by_country_per_capita.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Camels_by_country_per_capita.png/500px-Camels_by_country_per_capita.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACamels_by_country_per_capita.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG/500px-2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG/1280px-2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG/500px-2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2011_Trampeltier_1528.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Camelus_dromedarius_at_Tierpark_Berlin_%281%29.JPG/500px-Came